# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_self_heal_freshness.py" "SELF-HEAL FRESHNESS GATE: PASS" "self-heal advances the freshness coordinate (kill the perpetual graph_stale on a re-ingested coordinate)" "self-heal x freshness: after the boot/PR-time self-heal RE-INGESTS main's graph, the FRESHNESS coordinate the operator watches (the /freshz + /readyz body and the stale-graph alert input) ADVANCES to the re-ingested HEAD sha -- so /freshz never pages behind:True with an ever-growing age FOREVER on a coordinate that has actually been re-ingested. Driven over a real scratch Postgres through the REAL functions (self_heal_main_graph -> ingest_push -> _full_ingest -> core.ingest_graph_with_authority, freshness read via graph_freshness / graph_freshness_all): ingest @A => fresh at A behind=False; main HEAD moves to B but the push is MISSED => stale at A behind=True (the drift); self_heal re-ingests @HEAD => the coordinate now reads B behind=False with a fresh ingested_at, AND the /freshz surface resolves (not a perpetual stale page). CONSISTENCY: the normal push-ingest advances the SAME coordinate too, so push and self-heal can never drift to where only one freshens freshness. content-free (a commit sha is public git metadata + a timestamp), moat unchanged, fail-open (a freshness-update error never crashes the ingest)" "self-heal x freshness: a self-heal re-ingest ADVANCES the freshness coordinate to the re-ingested HEAD (stale-at-A before, fresh-at-B after, behind=False) so the perpetual graph_stale alert dies the moment a re-ingest happens; the normal push path advances the same coordinate too; content-free, moat unchanged, fail-open" 24
